item.p:
terms and conditions of employment means the mandatory provisions of the Swiss Code of Obligations

  SR 220
	 concerning the employment contract, normative provisions of collective and standard employment contracts or, in the absence of these, the employment conditions customary in the place of work and in the sector;

administrative units of the central and decentralised Federal Administration in accordance with Article 2 of the Federal Act of 21 March 1997

  SR 172.010
	 on the Organisation of the Government and the Administration and the associated implementing provisions that apply at the time of the invitation to tender;

the provision of postal services in the reserved services area in accordance with the Postal Services Act of 17 December 2010

  SR 783.0
	;

the granting of financial assistance in accordance with the Federal Act of 5 October 1990

  SR 616.1
	 on Financial Assistance and Subsidies;

type of contract and procedure and the relevant CPV
CPV = Common procurement vocabulary of the European Union classification, as well as the relevant CPC
CPC = Central product classification of the United Nations classification in the case of services;

has not resolved a vulnerability in the hard- or software it produces within the period stipulated by the National Cyber Security Centre in accordance with Article 73b paragraph 3 of the Information Security Act of 18 December 2020

 SR 128
	;

violated reporting or authorisation obligations under the IEA

  SR 822.41
	;
